# With `mutation 1 / 1` every gene of every child moves one step up or down
# (a sixteenth of the range, at least 1), never out of its range. Selection
# does the rest: a budder that looks less far counts fewer neighbours, so it
# keeps budding where one with a long `reach` stops. A line that starts at
# `reach` 9 is pulled down, and the world fills with short-sighted budders.
rules ../../packs/genes
seed 3
size 128 128
terrain water_level 0 rock_on_soil 0 rock_on_water 0   # flat soil everywhere
mutation 1 / 1
start budder at (62, 62) with (reach = 9)

run 3d
expect born budder > 1000
expect mean reach of budder < 5
expect min reach of budder >= 1
expect max reach of budder <= 10
